    "q-111305": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111305",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n\nLet $Y=2{X}^{2}-2.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $a$ | $b$ | $6$ | $16$ | $30$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.3$ | $c$ | $d$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $c-a?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y=2{X}^{2}-2$ row to our table:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $6$ | $16$ | $30$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $6$ | $16$ | $30$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n\nTherefore, $a=-2,$ $c=0.1,$ and $c-a=2.1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
