    "q-111308": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111308",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.3$ | $0.35$ | $0.1$ |\n\nLet $Y=5-2{X}^{2}.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $-13$ | $a$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $d$ | $b$ | $c$ | $0.25$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $a-c?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y=5-2{X}^{2}$ row to our table:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $5$ | $3$ | $-3$ | $-13$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.25$ | $0.3$ | $0.35$ | $0.1$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $-13$ | $-3$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.1$ | $0.35$ | $0.3$ | $0.25$ |\n\nTherefore, $a=-3,$ $c=0.3,$ and $a-c=-3.3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
