    "q-111310": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111310",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ | $0.2$ |\n\nLet $Y=3{X}^{2}+1.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $a$ | $13$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $b$ | $0.5$ | $c$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $ac?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y=3{X}^{2}+1$ row to our table:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $4$ | $13$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ | $0.2$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $4$ | $13$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ | $0.2$ |\n\nTherefore, $a=4,$ $c=0.2,$ and $ac=0.8.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
