    "q-111321": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111321",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ | $0.3$ |\n\nLet $Y=3{X}^{2}.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $a$ | $b$ | $12$ | $27$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.3$ | $c$ | $0.15$ | $d$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $b+c?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y=3{X}^{2}$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $27$ | $12$ | $3$ | $0$ | $3$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ | $0.3$ |\n\nFrom the table, we see that $Y\\in \\{0,3,12,27\\}.$ Notice that we now have two columns for $Y=3.$\n\nWe calculate the probabilities associated with each value of $Y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=0) & =0.3 \\\\ P(Y=3) & =0.15+0.3 \\\\ P(Y=12) & =0.15 \\\\ P(Y=27) & =0.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the following table.\n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $3$ | $12$ | $27$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.3$ | $0.45$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ |\n\nTherefore, $b=3,c=0.45,$ and $b+c=3.45.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
