    "q-111326": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111326",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ | $0.3$ | $0.3$ |\n\nLet $Y=2{X}^{2}+2.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $2$ | $a$ | $34$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $c$ | $d$ | $0.15$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $a+d?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y=2{X}^{2}+2$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-4$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $34$ | $10$ | $2$ | $10$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ | $0.3$ | $0.3$ |\n\nFrom the table, we see that $Y\\in \\{2,10,34\\}.$ Notice that we now have two columns for $Y=10.$\n\nWe calculate the probabilities associated with each value of $Y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=2) & =0.3 \\\\ P(Y=10) & =0.25+0.3 \\\\ P(Y=34) & =0.15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the following table.\n\n| $y$ | $2$ | $10$ | $34$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.3$ | $0.55$ | $0.15$ |\n\nTherefore, $a=10,d=0.55,$ and $a+d=10.55.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
