    "q-111323": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111323",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.5$ | $0.2$ | $0.15$ | $0.15$ |\n\nLet $Y={X}^{4}-4.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $a$ | $b$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.15$ | $c$ | $d$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $c-a?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y={X}^{4}-4$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $12$ | $-3$ | $-4$ | $-3$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.5$ | $0.2$ | $0.15$ | $0.15$ |\n\nFrom the table, we see that $Y\\in \\{-4,-3,12\\}.$ Notice that we now have two columns for $Y=-3.$\n\nWe calculate the probabilities associated with each value of $Y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=-4) & =0.15 \\\\ P(Y=-3) & =0.2+0.15 \\\\ P(Y=12) & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the following table.\n\n| $y$ | $-4$ | $-3$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.15$ | $0.35$ | $0.5$ |\n\nTherefore, $a=-4,c=0.35,$ and $c-a=4.35.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-111323-a",
