    "q-111313": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111313",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ |\n\nLet $Y=1-{X}^{2}.$ The distribution of $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $y$ | $a$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.4$ | $b$ | $c$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $b-a?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y=1-{X}^{2}$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-3$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we see that $Y\\in \\{-3,0,1\\}.$ Notice that we now have two columns for both $Y=-3$ and $Y=0.$\n\nWe calculate the probabilities associated with each value of $Y$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=-3) & =0.3+0.1 \\\\ P(Y=0) & =0.1+0.2 \\\\ P(Y=1) & =0.3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the following table.\n\n| $y$ | $-3$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.4$ | $0.3$ | $0.3$ |\n\nTherefore, $a=-3,b=0.3,$ and $b-a=3.3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
