      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ |\n\nCalculate $P({X}^{2}=4).$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's first calculate the distribution of ${X}^{2}:$\n\n| ${x}^{2}$ | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $9$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.05$ | $0.05$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we can immediately conclude that $P({X}^{2}=4)=0.3.$",
