    "q-110188": {
      "dom_id": "step-q110188",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ |\n\nCalculate $P({X}^{2}\\ge 3).$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's first add an ${X}^{2}$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}$ | $4$ | $1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third rows of our table, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({X}^{2}\\ge 3) & =P({X}^{2}=4) \\\\  & =0.2+0.4 \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
