    "q-110221": {
      "dom_id": "step-q110221",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "The random variable $X$ has the following probability distribution.\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $-\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n\nCalculate $P({X}^{2}\\ge 5).$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's first add an ${X}^{2}$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-3$ | $-\\sqrt{3}$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt{3}$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}$ | $9$ | $3$ | $0$ | $3$ | $9$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third rows of our table, we conclude that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({X}^{2}\\ge 5) & =P({X}^{2}=9) \\\\  & =0.3+0.2 \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
